{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387260-your-anime-inspirations-list","id":1387260,"title":"Your Anime Inspirations list","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-05-10T06:38:22-07:00","id":1387260,"title":"Your Anime Inspirations list","content":"Just like the title stated","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12378-fma245","name":"FMA245","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"165"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T13:55:45-07:00","id":1387322,"title":"","content":"All of them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8877-mrfamiliar","name":"MrFamiliar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"76"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T22:00:04-07:00","id":1387411,"title":"","content":"I'd probably start with Berserk, Fushigi Yuugi, Slayers, and Inuyasha. I'm probably dating myself a smidge with those.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T22:13:05-07:00","id":1387414,"title":"","content":"Do you mind if they're redundant with ones already in the books from various editions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T04:52:48-07:00","id":1387446,"title":"","content":"Definitely &quot;Record of Lodoss War&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8890-nullapostle","name":"NullApostle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T05:26:31-07:00","id":1387455,"title":"","content":"I like a bit tower of God. I've read the manwha a while ago, and it's getting an anime adaptation. I think all the stuff with the Jahad family being godlike and the rankers compared to the rest of the people show the difference between mortals and Exalted","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T09:04:32-07:00","id":1387509,"title":"","content":"Record of the Lodoss War was a great anime and a good game, Bleach (all honesty, Ichigo is how I build unwoven coadjuators, the way he interacts with Zangetsu and his inner hollow), Overlord is awesome for seeing how a celestial level exalted may act should they end up transported to a new land, I don't like Gundamn that much but I could def see it being awesome if you want inspiration for mech warfare or Alchemical inspiration before they turn into cities, chrome shelled regios is good if you want to get some inspiration on how Alchemicals work in cities and balance jobs on top of being heroes. there are so many anime shows out there that you could watch for inspiration though","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/359-dezeroth","name":"Dezeroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar359_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"496"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T09:33:28-07:00","id":1387518,"title":"","content":"Magi is a really good anime as well, great if you want to have some inspiration for evocations and giving your weapons some personality","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/359-dezeroth","name":"Dezeroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar359_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"496"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T10:17:19-07:00","id":1387534,"title":"","content":"Katanagatari is very good also. I think it can gives a lot of inspiration for Martial Art style characters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T11:27:13-07:00","id":1387548,"title":"","content":"Mushishi is really good inspiration for &quot;weird shit&quot; that you might see in Creation. The setting involves tiny nature spirits that do all kinds of weird things. Sometimes humans interact with them and bad things happen just because the spirits don't &quot;understand&quot; humans or aren't really capable of rational thought in the first place. It's not hard to take something from the show and use it as inspiration to create a spirit or elemental in Creation, and use it to highlight one of the small ways in which Creation is different from the real world, and is filled with strange and wondrous things. Probably of all of the anime/manga series I've checked out, it's the one I've mined the most for ideas for Exalted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-15T18:46:42-07:00","id":1388818,"title":"","content":"Full Metal Alchemist (the original)has neat examples for sorcery, and the consequences of trying to violate its limits.<br /> <br /> I enjoyed that anime so much that I've struggled to enjoy other anime since.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-15T18:51:14-07:00","id":1388819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tytalus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387260-your-anime-inspirations-list?p=1388818#post1388818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Full Metal Alchemist (the original)has neat examples for sorcery, and the consequences of trying to violate its limits.</div> </div> </div> </div> <b>Sister:</b> Oh cool, you have a dog?<br /> <br /> <b>Tucker:</b> Uh, that's not a dog, that's my kid.<br /> <br /> <b>Sister:</b> Oh, cool, you have a kid that looks like a dog?<br /> <br /> <b>Church:</b> Nice save.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T14:33:50-07:00","id":1391264,"title":"","content":"Avatar: The Last Airbender - PERFECT inspiration for how Spirits and Elementals work in Exalted. While its status as anime is contentious at best? It's so anime adjacent it deserves to be mentioned, as most anime fans have PROBABLY given it a shot. Hell, my local anime con didn't think twice about letting it be a fan suite, or even given said suite first place.<br /> <br /> Fuushigi Yuugi - definitely works, old or not.<br /> <br /> Yona of the Dawn - if nothing else the visuals, and a bit of Lunars and other stuff too.<br /> <br /> Chaika: Coffin Princess - Hardcore into the Magitech and such. It's not nearly as Abyssal sounding as the name implies, Chaika's more Twilight Caste Solar than anything. But holy crap does the Magitech feature! Very good visual inspiration.<br /> <br /> Scrapped Princess - Same author as Chaika, IIRC. And pretty similar comments. It's very Magitech full.<br /> <br /> Escaflowne - Where do you think War Walkers came from?<br /> <br /> I'll second Berserk and Slayers! They were a big way I sold it back in 1e. Heck, the first game I ran had a blatant Guts and a Lina Inverse ripoff in them.<br /> <br /> Heroic Legend of Arslan - Definitely the less personally powerful side, but the epic side for sure.<br /> <br /> Demon Slayer - A bit of Lunars and such for the Demon Side. And the main chars are very Solar-like. Or Dragonblooded. Great stunt inspiration for what Charms could look like too.<br /> <br /> Rokka: Braves of the Six Flowers - Very Mesoamerican based fantasy, and perfect inspiration for Lunars and Solars alike. This has some great visuals of a non-Western fantasy. Not to mention cool powers!<br /> <br /> It really is weird that it is hard to find more recent inspirations, but also kind of understandable given how much the Isekai genre has taken over the fantasy side of anime. Though even then?<br /> <br /> Konosuba - yeah, ok. It's STUPID. But let's not lie to ourselves, this is what most of our groups end up as. Megumin is the Twilight that went ALL IN on the best spell she could... and can cast it once before she's useless. Darkness has ALL the defensive charms, but nothing else, really. And then there's all the Magitech stuff in it. Hell, some of the villains and such would be great inspiration for Death Knights, Fae, and the likes.<br /> <br /> Princess Connect - This season, and perhaps even MORE stupid than Konosuba. From the same creator too. And great examples of Beastfolk in it too.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":448,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/448-dulahan","user":"Dulahan","date":". 05-24-2020, 05:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/448-dulahan","name":"Dulahan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar448_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"115"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-21T05:51:27-07:00","id":1397964,"title":"","content":"Just noticed this thread. Hmmm...In/Spectre is a good portrayal of interacting with spirits for the non-exalted might be like. <br /> Ruroni Kenshin for that badass Single Point Dawn you've wanted to build.<br /> Black Lagoon for how I see Nexus.<br /> My Hero Academia for no other reason than Deku vs Chisaki (overhaul) as what I see a knock down drag out fight between a master solar brawler and a very, very badass lunar with all sorts of shifting and mutations.<br /> Samurai Champloo...Lookshyan style Ronin and Outcaste swordmaster collide!<br /> Saiyuki cuz that's my group in a nutshell.<br /> The Hero Is Overpowered but Overly Cautious because there's always one in every damn group.<br /> God of the Highschool when it gets released cuz I've read the webtoon and this is Exalted Martial Arts!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24445-arkayriel","name":"Arkayriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"122"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-22T11:36:43-07:00","id":1398207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387260-your-anime-inspirations-list?p=1388819#post1388819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <b>Sister:</b> Oh cool, you have a dog?<br /> <br /> <b>Tucker:</b> Uh, that's not a dog, that's my kid.<br /> <br /> <b>Sister:</b> Oh, cool, you have a kid that looks like a dog?<br /> <br /> <b>Church:</b> Nice save.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now now don't be too mean here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-22T14:38:49-07:00","id":1398238,"title":"","content":"RWBY. The dynamic combat is very, very fun to watch, and it is what my Exalted combats look like in my imagination. I suggest starting with the trailers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-22T15:32:55-07:00","id":1398249,"title":"","content":"Another one - on the Anime-adjacent side because it's actually a donghua - a Chinese Anime, essentially.<br /> <br /> Mo Dao Zu Shi - The main character is basically a kung fu necromancer. There's a scene at the end of the first season that's just RIDICULOUSLY awesome inspiration for what I could see a powerful Abyssal looking like. Creepy, zombies, descending while playing a flute as green fires glow. Frankly, if this show doesn't end up being some good inspiration for Abyssals going forward, there is no justice in the world!<br /> <br /> Even better, it's legit available on Youtube because the company put it there! Plus it's a beautiful almost ink painting style of backgrounds animated. And the fight scenes are just amazingly well done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/448-dulahan","name":"Dulahan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar448_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"115"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-22T18:09:27-07:00","id":1398266,"title":"","content":"Do RWBY, AtLA and SPoP count as Anime?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-22T19:44:59-07:00","id":1398277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387260-your-anime-inspirations-list?p=1398266#post1398266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do RWBY, AtLA and SPoP count as Anime?</div> </div> </div> </div>SPoP is what now?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-22T21:28:50-07:00","id":1398285,"title":"","content":"She ra and the Princesses of Power","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-25T05:18:32-07:00","id":1398755,"title":"","content":"Hmm. Hard to say. Some things have long merged into the background of how I process my characters and games. <br /> <br /> For my heaven's reach game, The Pretty Reckless are basically living the same kind of shenanigans as the Bebop crew.<br /> For our blessed isle game, whatever it started as we have slowly transitioned to something more akin to Akatsuki no Yona because at some point the three sidereals' shenanigans revolving around our rebellious fire aspect dynast meshed well with the couple times we snuck some sense in her cantankerous head.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> And that's about it. The spy/war/doom game I'm running doesn't draw particularly from anything I can immediately link to an anime. My dawn syndrome Sword Muse is basically Super Greek La Maupin after she ate an elf. My Mars sid is almost literally a witcher. Final Countdown is an unholy, well dressed mix of John Wick and Hackerman.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-26T03:19:29-07:00","id":1398994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387260-your-anime-inspirations-list?p=1398266#post1398266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do RWBY, AtLA and SPoP count as Anime?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This is a deceptively simple question over which a lot of digital ink has been spilled. Is it Champagne if it comes from California? well, to a Purist, no. It has to come from France. But to people who like Champagne, yeah, its Champagne and bickering over technicalities doesn't change the fact that it walks like a duck and quacks like a duck. I'm of the mind that &quot;Anime&quot; has escaped being a media type and become a Genre- we can all identify 'anime tropes' and if you make something in the 'anime style' then yeah, its anime. <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/448-dulahan\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar448_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"448\" data-vbnamecard=\"448\">Dulahan</a> I watched the first episode because you mentioned it, and <i>holy shit</i>, this is Exalted as fuck.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-26T13:46:53-07:00","id":1399131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387260-your-anime-inspirations-list?p=1398994#post1398994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/448-dulahan\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar448_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"448\" data-vbnamecard=\"448\">Dulahan</a> I watched the first episode because you mentioned it, and <i>holy shit</i>, this is Exalted as fuck.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seriously! Exactly why I suggested it here. It's just beyond ridiculous how many cool things are in it that apply.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/448-dulahan","name":"Dulahan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar448_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"115"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-26T21:44:06-07:00","id":1399203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387260-your-anime-inspirations-list?p=1398266#post1398266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do RWBY, AtLA and SPoP count as Anime?</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically, it's only anime if it comes from the Anime region of Japan. Otherwise, it's just sparkling cartoons. XD<br /> <br /> On topic:<br /> *Thunderbolt Fantasy (puppets and not animation, but goddammit it counts)<br /> *Rising of the Shield Hero (especially good depiction of beastmen and a very weird world full of magic)<br /> *Danganronpa (what social combat looks like)<br /> *Jigoku Shoujo (Abyssals all the way)<br /> *Sengoku Basara (a great depiction of Exalted-level combat)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />&quot;The true object of all human life is play. Earth is a task garden; heaven is a playground.&quot; -G.K. Chesterton","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/53-blackwingedheaven","name":"blackwingedheaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar53_3.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-27T00:54:17-07:00","id":1399227,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Rising of the Shield Hero (especially good depiction of beastmen and a very weird world full of magic) </div> </div> </div>Less good is the pro-slavery perspective in the first episode. I couldn\u2019t really get further into it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-27T04:35:00-07:00","id":1399252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387260-your-anime-inspirations-list?p=1399227#post1399227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Less good is the pro-slavery perspective in the first episode. I couldn\u2019t really get further into it.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's one of the popular isekai tropes I could do without. All about the power fantasy, I guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8890-nullapostle","name":"NullApostle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-28T06:32:35-07:00","id":1399585,"title":"","content":"<di